 202:../src/miv_rv32_hal/miv_rv32_hal.c ****      *
 203:../src/miv_rv32_hal/miv_rv32_hal.c ****      * Please ensure that interrupt handlers are as short as possible to prevent
 204:../src/miv_rv32_hal/miv_rv32_hal.c ****      * them stopping other interrupts from being handled. For example, if a
 205:../src/miv_rv32_hal/miv_rv32_hal.c ****      * system timer interrupt occurs during a software interrupt, the system
 206:../src/miv_rv32_hal/miv_rv32_hal.c ****      * timer interrupt will not be handled until the software interrupt handling
 207:../src/miv_rv32_hal/miv_rv32_hal.c ****      * is complete. If the software interrupt handling time is more than one systick
 208:../src/miv_rv32_hal/miv_rv32_hal.c ****      * interval, it will result in d_tick > 1.
 209:../src/miv_rv32_hal/miv_rv32_hal.c ****      *
 210:../src/miv_rv32_hal/miv_rv32_hal.c ****      * If you are running the program using the debugger and halt the CPU at a breakpoint,
 211:../src/miv_rv32_hal/miv_rv32_hal.c ****      * MTIME will continue to increment and interrupts will be missed; resulting
 212:../src/miv_rv32_hal/miv_rv32_hal.c ****      * in d_tick > 1.
